1
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:15,020
On Saturday, 11 February 2012, the
night before the Grammy Awards,

2
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:19,120
Whitney Houston died at the Beverly
Hilton hotel in Beverly Hills,

3
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:20,224
California.

4
00:00:20,274 --> 00:00:21,699
She was forty-eight years old.

5
00:00:22,277 --> 00:00:24,982
This is the story of that day,
of the week that followed,

6
00:00:25,302 --> 00:00:26,842
and of what the official records say.

7
00:00:27,502 --> 00:00:28,682
Only what the records say.

8
00:00:29,258 --> 00:00:34,383
She was born in Newark, New Jersey, in 1963,
and she first sang in public in the choir

9
00:00:34,383 --> 00:00:38,083
of New Hope Baptist Church, the church
where her funeral would be held.

10
00:00:38,646 --> 00:00:43,306
In 1983 the record executive Clive
Davis saw her sing in a New York club,

11
00:00:43,506 --> 00:00:47,946
in her mother’s act. She was nineteen,
and he later said her voice shattered him.

12
00:00:55,738 --> 00:01:00,933
Her first album came out in 1985, and her
first seven singles to reach number one in

13
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:02,993
America followed within three years.

14
00:01:14,162 --> 00:01:19,547
In 1992 she starred in The Bodyguard, and
its soundtrack became one of the best-selling

15
00:01:19,547 --> 00:01:20,387
albums ever.

16
00:01:27,772 --> 00:01:32,267
In 2012 her official website said she had
sold more than one hundred and seventy million

17
00:01:32,267 --> 00:01:34,247
albums, singles and videos.

18
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,280
In 1994 she won the Grammy for Record
of the Year for I Will Always Love You,

19
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:41,360
and she sang it on that stage.

20
00:01:50,728 --> 00:01:53,613
In 2009 came her last
album, I Look to You.

21
00:01:54,233 --> 00:01:58,073
In early 2012 she was working
again, and she was in a new film,

22
00:01:58,213 --> 00:01:59,553
Sparkle, due that August.

23
00:02:00,249 --> 00:02:03,774
Clive Davis would tell her funeral that
she had visited him the week before,

24
00:02:04,054 --> 00:02:06,014
alone, to play him new songs.

25
00:02:27,095 --> 00:02:30,200
That weekend the Beverly Hilton was
the centre of the music industry,

26
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:34,480
because Clive Davis held his pre-Grammy
party there on the Saturday night.

27
00:02:34,983 --> 00:02:40,083
Houston was staying in room 434, according to
the Los Angeles County coroner’s case file,

28
00:02:40,503 --> 00:02:42,563
and the file gives the
afternoon in minutes.

29
00:02:43,319 --> 00:02:46,979
Her assistant last saw her alive between
a quarter to three and three o’clock,

30
00:02:47,359 --> 00:02:49,899
and told her it was time to start
getting ready for that night.

31
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:54,761
At about twenty-five to four, the assistant
came back and found her unresponsive.

32
00:02:55,425 --> 00:03:00,310
Emergency services were called at 3:43, and
paramedics determined that she had died at

33
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:01,910
3:55 in the afternoon.

34
00:03:02,588 --> 00:03:06,533
Just before five, Pacific time, the
Associated Press moved the news,

35
00:03:06,813 --> 00:03:08,393
after her publicist confirmed it.

36
00:03:19,267 --> 00:03:22,867
Beverly Hills police said there were
no obvious signs of criminal intent,

37
00:03:23,227 --> 00:03:26,967
and the next day the coroner’s office
said foul play was not suspected.

38
00:03:27,641 --> 00:03:31,081
In the same hotel that night,
the Clive Davis party went ahead.

39
00:03:31,656 --> 00:03:34,296
Davis told the room he
was personally devastated,

40
00:03:34,796 --> 00:03:38,756
asked for a moment of silence, and said
she would have wanted the music to go on.

41
00:03:39,338 --> 00:03:43,058
Tony Bennett performed first and called
her the greatest singer he had ever heard.

42
00:03:43,818 --> 00:03:46,778
Alicia Keys sang No One for
her, while Brandy and Monica,

43
00:03:47,058 --> 00:03:49,818
who were close to Houston, were
too heart-stricken to perform.

44
00:03:50,413 --> 00:03:53,258
The producer Jimmy Jam called
it a bittersweet irony,

45
00:03:53,478 --> 00:03:56,838
because that gala was where Clive
Davis had first introduced her.

46
00:03:57,350 --> 00:03:59,695
Some people criticised
the decision to carry on,

47
00:03:59,955 --> 00:04:02,315
and the singer Chaka Khan was one of them.

48
00:04:02,875 --> 00:04:05,715
Other reports said her family
had urged Davis to go ahead.

49
00:04:06,288 --> 00:04:11,228
The next night, at the Grammy Awards, the
host LL Cool J opened with a prayer for her,

50
00:04:11,468 --> 00:04:14,228
and Jennifer Hudson sang
I Will Always Love You,

51
00:04:14,428 --> 00:04:16,048
before about forty million viewers.

52
00:04:22,167 --> 00:04:25,127
The autopsy was completed
on Sunday, 12 February.

53
00:04:25,867 --> 00:04:28,407
The coroner’s office said
there were no signs of trauma,

54
00:04:29,007 --> 00:04:31,507
and that toxicology tests
would take six to eight weeks.

55
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:37,385
On 14 February, New Jersey Governor Chris
Christie said flags would fly at half-staff

56
00:04:37,385 --> 00:04:38,485
on the day of her funeral.

57
00:04:50,667 --> 00:04:53,507
The funeral was held on
Saturday, 18 February,

58
00:04:53,867 --> 00:04:55,447
at New Hope Baptist Church in Newark.

59
00:04:56,307 --> 00:04:59,127
It was invitation only, it
was planned for two hours,

60
00:04:59,627 --> 00:05:02,667
it ran for about four, and it
was carried live on television.

61
00:05:03,419 --> 00:05:06,359
Her mother, Cissy Houston, and
her daughter were in the church.

62
00:05:07,099 --> 00:05:10,759
Stevie Wonder, Alicia Keys, CeCe
Winans and Kim Burrell sang,

63
00:05:11,119 --> 00:05:15,059
and Kevin Costner, Clive Davis,
Dionne Warwick and Tyler Perry spoke.

64
00:05:15,704 --> 00:05:18,229
Costner, who starred with
her in The Bodyguard,

65
00:05:18,449 --> 00:05:21,489
told the church that the song
had almost not made the film.

66
00:05:22,112 --> 00:05:24,672
He said that they had both
grown up in the Baptist church,

67
00:05:25,212 --> 00:05:26,172
and that she had come home.

68
00:05:34,862 --> 00:05:36,167
Stevie Wonder played for her.

69
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,320
Then Clive Davis spoke, as the
man who had discovered her.

70
00:05:58,028 --> 00:05:59,393
He did not avoid the hard part.

71
00:05:59,873 --> 00:06:02,013
He said she had admitted
to crises in her life,

72
00:06:02,453 --> 00:06:04,633
and had confessed her
battles to Oprah Winfrey,

73
00:06:04,873 --> 00:06:06,713
and that when he needed
her, she was there.

74
00:06:21,228 --> 00:06:24,853
He called himself her industry father,
and said she was one of a kind.

75
00:06:25,469 --> 00:06:29,749
She was buried on 19 February at
Fairview Cemetery in Westfield,

76
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:31,509
New Jersey, next to her father.

77
00:06:32,249 --> 00:06:35,689
More than five million people
watched the service on CNN alone.

78
00:06:41,767 --> 00:06:44,227
What remained was the
question of how she died,

79
00:06:44,627 --> 00:06:49,787
and the answer came on 22 March 2012,
from the Los Angeles County coroner.

80
00:06:50,336 --> 00:06:52,321
The coroner ruled the
cause of death drowning,

81
00:06:52,721 --> 00:06:57,741
with the effects of atherosclerotic
heart disease and cocaine use.

82
00:06:58,541 --> 00:07:00,161
The manner of death was accident.

83
00:07:00,842 --> 00:07:04,022
The office said cocaine and
its metabolites contributed.

84
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:09,162
Marijuana and three medicines,
Xanax, Flexeril and Benadryl,

85
00:07:09,342 --> 00:07:12,342
were found, and the coroner
said they did not contribute.

86
00:07:12,969 --> 00:07:15,094
There was no trauma and no foul play.

87
00:07:15,694 --> 00:07:18,874
A coroner’s spokesman said there
were signs of chronic cocaine use.

88
00:07:19,465 --> 00:07:22,050
The full case report, with
the times of that afternoon,

89
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:25,370
was released in April, and the
times in this film come from it.

90
00:07:25,822 --> 00:07:27,742
Her family said it was
saddened by the results,

91
00:07:28,142 --> 00:07:29,022
and glad to have closure.

92
00:07:29,673 --> 00:07:32,428
She had spoken publicly about
her struggles with drugs,

93
00:07:32,948 --> 00:07:35,048
including to Oprah Winfrey in 2009.

94
00:07:35,812 --> 00:07:37,952
That is everything the
official record says:

95
00:07:38,752 --> 00:07:41,932
a time, a place, a cause,
and a ruling of accident.

96
00:07:42,832 --> 00:07:45,392
It does not say more, and
this film will not guess.

97
00:07:46,144 --> 00:07:51,944
On 16 November 2012, CBS broadcast a
tribute concert from the Recording Academy,

98
00:07:52,544 --> 00:07:56,144
with Celine Dion, Usher,
Jennifer Hudson and many others.

99
00:07:56,825 --> 00:08:01,725
Her last film, Sparkle, opened that August,
and her songs are still played every day.

100
00:08:08,345 --> 00:08:11,630
The record gives us a time,
a cause and a funeral.

101
00:08:12,350 --> 00:08:15,230
When you remember Whitney
Houston, which do you hear first:

102
00:08:15,490 --> 00:08:16,890
the last day, or the voice?
